        "model_answer": "Regimen: 2 months Intensive Phase of HRZE (Isoniazid, Rifampicin, Pyrazinamide, Ethambutol) followed by 4 months Continuation Phase of HR (extended to 9 months total if cavitary + culture positive at 2 months, especially in diabetics). Co-prescribe Pyridoxine (Vitamin B6 10-25mg OD) with Isoniazid. Toxicities: 1. Isoniazid -> peripheral neuropathy & hepatitis; 2. Rifampicin -> orange body fluids, CYP450 enzyme induction, hepatitis; 3. Pyrazinamide -> hyperuricaemia/gout flare & hepatitis; 4. Ethambutol -> retrobulbar optic neuritis (check Snellen visual acuity & Ishihara colour vision before starting!).",
