        "model_answer": "Acute management: 1. Sit patient upright; 2. Non-Invasive Ventilation (CPAP / BiPAP) early to recruit alveoli and reduce LV preload/afterload; 3. IV Loop Diuretic: IV Frusemide 40–80mg STAT (at least 1–2x her home oral daily dose) with urinary catheter chart; 4. IV GTN (Glyceryl Trinitrate) infusion since SBP is 168 mmHg (>110 mmHg) for venodilation/afterload reduction (avoid routine Morphine!). Long-term 4 Pillars of HFrEF (mortality-reducing): 1) ARNI (Sacubitril/Valsartan) or ACEi/ARB, 2) Evidence-based Beta-blocker (Bisoprolol/Carvedilol/Metoprolol succinate — start once euvolaemic), 3) MRA (Spironolactone/Eplerenone), 4) SGLT2 inhibitor (Dapagliflozin/Empagliflozin).",
