        "model_answer": "Initiate a Direct Oral Anticoagulant (DOAC: Apixaban 5mg BD, Rivaroxaban 20mg OD, or Dabigatran) immediately after checking renal/liver function and HAS-BLED score. DOACs are preferred over Warfarin in non-valvular AF (lower intracranial haemorrhage risk, no INR monitoring). Aspirin monotherapy is ineffective for cardioembolic left atrial appendage thrombus prophylaxis and carries similar major bleeding risk in the elderly.",
