        "question": "Describe the 6 steps of the SPIKES protocol for breaking bad news.",
        "prompt": "Describe the 6 steps of the SPIKES protocol for breaking bad news.",
        "model_answer": "S - Setting up the interview (private room, uninterrupted, key relatives present, sit down without physical barriers); P - Assessing the patient's Perception ('What do you understand so far?'); I - Obtaining the patient's Invitation ('How much detail would you like to hear today?'); K - Giving Knowledge and information (warning shot: 'Unfortunately the results are more serious than we hoped', clear plain English, chunk and check); E - Addressing the patient's Emotions with empathic responses (NURSE: Naming, Understanding, Respecting, Supporting, Exploring); S - Strategy and Summary (clear medical plan, oncology/MDT referral, emergency contacts, early follow-up).",
        "target_rubric": "S - Setting up the interview (private room, uninterrupted, key relatives present, sit down without physical barriers); P - Assessing the patient's Perception ('What do you understand so far?'); I - Obtaining the patient's Invitation ('How much detail would you like to hear today?'); K - Giving Knowledge and information (warning shot: 'Unfortunately the results are more serious than we hoped', clear plain English, chunk and check); E - Addressing the patient's Emotions with empathic responses (NURSE: Naming, Understanding, Respecting, Supporting, Exploring); S - Strategy and Summary (clear medical plan, oncology/MDT referral, emergency contacts, early follow-up).",
