        "model_answer": "1. Acknowledge and validate the daughter's loving, protective intention; 2. Gently explain that every competent adult patient has an ethical and legal right to information regarding their own diagnosis to make autonomous medical decisions; 3. Explore the family's specific cultural or emotional fears; 4. Reassure the daughter that bad news is delivered sensitively and paced according to the mother's readiness; 5. Inquire directly with the patient in the room how much information she wishes to receive today, honoring her autonomy to delegate decision-making if she explicitly chooses.",
