        "prompt": "Identify the red flags for Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD) in a toddler, and outline the multidisciplinary referral and early intervention pathway in Singapore.",
        "model_answer": "ASD Red Flags: 1. Lack of joint attention (not pointing to share enjoyment/interest by 14-18 months); 2. Poor or fleeting eye contact; 3. Lack of response to name by 12 months; 4. Absence of pretend/symbolic play; 5. Stereotypic, repetitive behaviors (lining up toys, spinning objects, hand flapping) or insistence on sameness; 6. Regression or loss of previously acquired language/social skills at any age. Referral pathway in Singapore: 1. Formal Audiology (BERA/tympanometry to rule out hearing loss); 2. Polyclinic referral to Child Development Unit (KKH CDU or NUH Child Development Clinic); 3. Enrollment into Early Intervention Programme for Infants & Children (EIPIC); 4. Speech and Language Therapy (SLT) + Occupational Therapy (OT); 5. Parental counseling to eliminate screen time (<2h/day) and foster interactive parent-child play.",
