        "prompt": "Formulate the acute resuscitation and long-term medical and surgical management options for this 44yo woman.",
        "model_answer": "1. Acute resuscitation: Blood transfusion with 2 units Packed Red Blood Cells (target Hb >8 g/dL for symptomatic Hb 6.4) + IV Iron replacement (Ferric carboxymaltose) + Oral Tranexamic acid (1g TDS during menses) to reduce acute menstrual blood loss; 2. Medical management: Levonorgestrel-releasing Intrauterine System (LNG-IUS / Mirena — first-line, reduces blood loss by 70-90% if cavity allows), Oral Progestogens, or GnRH agonists/antagonists (e.g. Leuprorelin / Relugolix) as short-term bridge to surgery to shrink fibroid volume and restore Hb; 3. Surgical options: Transcervical Resection of Myoma (TCRM for submucosal component), Laparoscopic/Open Myomectomy (fertility-sparing), Uterine Artery Embolization (UAE), or Total Laparoscopic Hysterectomy (definitive cure with zero recurrence, since family is complete).",
