        "prompt": "How does HHS differ biochemically and pathophysiologically from DKA, and why do you start IV 0.9% NaCl BEFORE starting IV Insulin in pure HHS?",
        "model_answer": "In Type 2 DM (HHS), residual basal endogenous insulin is sufficient to suppress lipolysis/ketogenesis (pH >7.30, ketones <3.0) but insufficient to prevent severe hyperglycemia (>30 mmol/L) and osmotic diuresis (osmolality >320 mOsm/kg). Starting IV 0.9% NaCl FIRST lowers glucose safely by hemodilution/renal perfusion; starting insulin before fluid resuscitation drives glucose and water INTO cells, precipitating cardiovascular collapse/shock and rapid osmolality shifts (pontine myelinolysis/cerebral edema).",
