        "prompt": "Outline your immediate management plan for Infantile Hypertrophic Pyloric Stenosis.",
        "model_answer": "1. NBM + NG tube aspiration; 2. Resuscitate dehydration and correct electrolyte abnormality FIRST using IV 0.45% or 0.9% Sodium Chloride + 5% Dextrose + KCl (20 mmol/L) until serum Cl- >100 mmol/L and HCO3 <26-28 mmol/L; 3. Once biochemically corrected: Ramstedt's Pyloromyotomy (longitudinal splitting of hypertrophied circular muscle leaving mucosa intact).",
