        "model_answer": "Viral Croup (Parainfluenza): Preceding viral coryza, loud barking cough, hoarse voice, low-grade fever, able to swallow. Epiglottitis (H. influenzae type b): Sudden onset, toxic 40°C fever, muffled 'hot potato' voice, NO barking cough, tripod position, and profuse DROOLING (dysphagia). Agitating the child increases respiratory distress and narrows the subglottic airway.",
