        "model_answer": "1. Keep child calm on parent's lap with minimal handling (NO tongue depressor, NO routine bloods/X-rays); 2. Single dose Oral Dexamethasone 0.15 - 0.6 mg/kg STAT (or Nebulised Budesonide 2mg / IM Dexamethasone if vomiting) — mandatory for ALL severities of croup; 3. Since stridor at rest is present: Nebulised Adrenaline (Epinephrine 1:1000, 0.5 mL/kg up to 5 mL) + humidified O2; 4. Observe for >= 4 hours after nebulised Adrenaline to ensure no rebound stridor before discharge.",
