        "model_answer": "90% of paracetamol undergoes safe glucuronidation/sulfation, while ~5-10% is metabolized by CYP2E1 into the toxic reactive metabolite NAPQI, which is normally detoxified by hepatic Glutathione. In overdose, Glutathione stores are depleted and unbound NAPQI causes Centrilobular (Zone 3) hepatic necrosis. NAC replenishes hepatic Glutathione (and acts as a direct sulfhydryl donor). King's College Criteria for super-urgent Liver Transplant: Arterial pH < 7.30 after resuscitation (alone), OR all 3 of: PT > 100s (INR > 6.5) + Creatinine > 300 umol/L + Grade III/IV Hepatic Encephalopathy.",
