        "model_answer": "1. Activated Charcoal (50g PO) ONLY if presenting within <1-2 hours of ingestion (not indicated at 5h); 2. Plot >=4-hour Paracetamol level on Rumack-Matthew nomogram (or start immediately without waiting for level if staggered overdose or >8 hours post-ingestion!); 3. Administer IV N-Acetylcysteine (NAC, SNAP 12-hour regimen: 100 mg/kg over 2h then 200 mg/kg over 10h, or traditional 21h 3-bag regimen); 4. Recheck ALT, INR, Creatinine & VBG at end of NAC + Mandatory Inpatient Psychiatric Suicide Risk Assessment.",
